# Benchmark output. Every run writes one JSON here plus a resumable checkpoint;
# reference numbers that are meant to be committed live in reference-results/.
benchmark-results/

# data/images/ is deliberately NOT ignored — the 841 screenshots are committed, so a
# clone is everything you need. If a v2 corpus ever replaces them, remember that the v1
# blobs stay in history: PNGs do not delta-compress, and the only way to drop them is a
# force-push that breaks every existing clone and fork.
